Subject: [PATCH 11168/11362] [outer-loop] A supervisor arm regains eligibility
 each level (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7040)

The force-diversity arm could only fire once per RUN inside a table designed to
reset per LEVEL. The supervisor clears _arms_used on every level-up, so its
table believed the arm was free again; the arm's guard reads
explorer._hybrid_diversity, which was set at init from the environment and set
True when the arm fired, and no line anywhere set it back. Every level after
the first ran a rung short, and every deep level in the refinement ledger's
five exhaustion cells was missing exactly this arm.

That also explains a downstream confusion: deep levels could never fire the
full ladder, so they never satisfied 'every enabled arm fired', and the
exhaustion trigger survived on level 0 alone while the pooled arm set hid it.

Found by the adversarial reviewer on the unmerged round-two branch, but the bug
is on main and predates that branch, so it is fixed here and does not wait on
the merge decision.

Restores the OPERATOR BASELINE, never a bare False: a run started with
CARNOT_ARC_EXPLORE_DIVERSITY=1 asked for diversity throughout, and switching it
off at a level-up would be worse than the bug. Ordered before the snapshot,
because a restore the supervisor cannot see this tick is one it acts on a
window late. Both properties carry their own mutation.

Recorded honestly: two rounds of decorative tests happened here. The first
version tested a hand-written mirror of the rule, to dodge the memory watchdog
that refuses importing arc_competition_agent, and two mutations of the real
code survived because a mirror passes every mutation of what it mirrors. The
rule was extracted into a light module so the real function is importable. A
fifth mutation discarding the return value then still survived, since nothing
asserted the agent stores it, and discarding it silently converts a
once-per-level reset into an every-tick reset. 5 of 5 RED now, 8 tests.

